; Galactose VM Disk I/O Example
; This program writes a sequence of bytes to RAM,
; commits them to disk, then reads them back.

; --- Step 1: Prepare data in RAM ---
PUSH 104        ; ASCII 'h'
POP R1
RAM_STORE 0 R1  ; Write 'h' to RAM address 0

PUSH 101        ; ASCII 'e'
POP R1
RAM_STORE 1 R1  ; Write 'e' to RAM address 1

PUSH 121        ; ASCII 'y'
POP R1
RAM_STORE 2 R1  ; Write 'y' to RAM address 2

; --- Step 2: Write to Disk ---
PUSH 0          ; Start address in RAM
PUSH 3          ; Number of bytes to write
WRITE_DISK      ; Commits RAM[0:3] to disk.gsd

; --- Step 3: Clear RAM to prove read works ---
PUSH 0
POP R1
RAM_STORE 0 R1
RAM_STORE 1 R1
RAM_STORE 2 R1

; --- Step 4: Read from Disk ---
PUSH 0          ; Destination address in RAM
PUSH 3          ; Number of bytes to read
READ_DISK       ; Loads disk data into RAM[0:3]

; --- Step 5: Visual Verification (VRAM) ---
; Load from RAM and STORE to VRAM to see it on screen
LOAD R10 0      ; Load 'h' from RAM
STORE 0 R10     ; Display 'h' at VRAM 0

LOAD R11 1      ; Load 'e' from RAM
STORE 1 R11     ; Display 'e' at VRAM 1

LOAD R12 2      ; Load 'y' from RAM
STORE 2 R12     ; Display 'y' at VRAM 2

HALT
